      "id": "2lodpya",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "A. Agents of Erosion"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Erosion involves three main steps: detachment, transportation, and removal of weathered material by natural agents.",
        "The primary physical and chemical erosion processes include Hydraulic Action, Abrasion, Attrition, and Solution.",
        "River erosion progresses through distinct stages: Vertical Erosion (deepening in youth stage), Lateral Erosion (widening in mature stage), and Headward Erosion (backward cutting at river source).",
        "Sediment transportation takes place via Traction (rolling), Saltation (bouncing), Suspension (carried in water), and Solution (dissolved load).",
        "Base level represents the lowest point erosion can reach, with sea level acting as the ultimate base level."
      ],
      "id": "0khas4v"
    },
